E. Farmer profitability calculator

Calculate:

Total Production Cost = Sum of Recorded Crop Expenses.

Gross Sales Revenue = Sum of Sales Quantity × Actual Selling Price.

Estimated Crop Profit = Gross Sales Revenue − Recorded Production Costs.

Profit Margin = Estimated Crop Profit ÷ Gross Sales Revenue × 100, where revenue is greater than zero.

Cost per Unit = Recorded Production Costs ÷ Harvest Quantity, where harvest quantity is greater than zero.

Clearly state which costs are included and whether labor, transport, financing, and other expenses are complete.

Separate forecast figures from actual recorded results.

F. Harvest forecasting

Create a basic forecast using recorded planting dates, crop information, and manually entered estimates.

Display forecast confidence and limitations where feasible.

Do not claim advanced AI accuracy without sufficient real-world data and validation. Never present predictions as guaranteed harvests.

G. BioSoil integration

Allow farmers to browse approved BioSoil products, request quotations, place orders, and record product use on their farms.

Do not automatically recommend a particular compost or fertilizer application rate without reliable product information and appropriate agronomic guidance.

